BT /F2 16 Tf 56 762.8 Td (SMS-15 Incident and Near-Miss Reporting) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 720.7 Td (Shipboard SMS Procedure: Incident and Near-Miss Reporting) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 678.7 Td (Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 664.2 Td (This procedure establishes the mandatory protocols for reporting safety-related events) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 649.7 Td (aboard the vessel. The objective is to ensure immediate containment of hazards, accurate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 635.2 Td (data capture for root cause analysis, and continuous improvement of maritime safety) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 620.7 Td (standards. Strict adherence to these guidelines is required for all crew members, regardless) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 606.2 Td (of rank or department.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 564.1 Td (What to Report) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 549.6 Td (The scope of reportable events is comprehensive and non-negotiable. All injuries, spills,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 535.1 Td (near misses and equipment failures affecting safety must be reported. This includes minor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 520.6 Td (first-aid cases that do not require off-hire medical attention, as well as significant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 506.1 Td (environmental releases. Any malfunction of critical navigation, propulsion, or fire-fighting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 491.6 Td (systems constitutes a reportable equipment failure, even if the vessel remained operational.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 477.1 Td (Near-misses, defined as events where no injury, damage, or loss occurred but had the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 462.6 Td (potential to do so, are equally critical to document. The goal is total transparency; if an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 448.1 Td (event impacts safety, it must be logged.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 406.1 Td (Immediate Actions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 391.6 Td (Upon occurrence of any reportable event, the Officer of the Watch \(OOW\) or responsible) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 377.1 Td (department head must prioritize life safety and environmental protection. Secure the scene) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 362.6 Td (to prevent further harm or evidence contamination. If medical assistance is required,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 348.1 Td (initiate emergency protocols immediately. For spills, deploy containment booms or absorbents) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 333.6 Td (as per the Shipboard Oil Pollution Emergency Plan \(SOPEP\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 304.6 Td (For serious incidents, such as those involving significant injury, major pollution, or total) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 290.1 Td (loss of propulsion, immediate verbal notification is mandatory. Serious incidents are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 275.6 Td (reported to the Designated Person Ashore \(DPA\) by phone immediately. This call must provide) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 261.1 Td (a concise summary of the event, current status, and any immediate risks. Simultaneously,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 246.6 Td (preserve all relevant data, including VDR records, engine logs, CCTV footage, and witness) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 232.1 Td (statements. Do not alter or clean up the scene until authorized by the DPA or company) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 217.6 Td (management, unless safety dictates otherwise.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 175.5 Td (Reporting Timelines) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 161.0 Td (Timely reporting is essential for effective analysis and regulatory compliance. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 146.5 Td (following strict timelines apply to all crew members:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 117.5 Td (-   Serious Incidents: In addition to the immediate phone call, a detailed written report) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 103.0 Td (  must be submitted within 24 hours. This document should include chronological events,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 88.5 Td (  initial assessment, and preliminary corrective actions taken.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (SMS-15 Incident and Near-Miss Reporting \(fictional\) - page 1 of 2) Tj ET
