BT /F1 10 Tf 56 771.5 Td (-   Near-Misses: Near-miss reports are submitted within 72 hours in the reporting system.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 757.0 Td (  These reports should focus on the sequence of events and contributing factors rather) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 742.5 Td (  than blame.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 728.0 Td (-   General Incidents: All other reportable events, including minor injuries and equipment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 713.5 Td (  failures, must be logged in the vessel's internal safety management system within 48) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 699.0 Td (  hours of occurrence.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 670.0 Td (Delays in reporting without valid justification will result in disciplinary action. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 655.5 Td (Master is responsible for ensuring that all reports are accurate, complete, and submitted on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 641.0 Td (time.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 598.9 Td (Investigation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 584.4 Td (Investigations are conducted to identify root causes and prevent recurrence. Investigations) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 569.9 Td (of serious incidents start within 48 hours. A joint investigation team comprising the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 555.4 Td (Master, Chief Engineer, and Safety Officer will be formed for serious incidents. For near-) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 540.9 Td (misses, the department head may conduct a preliminary investigation, which is then reviewed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 526.4 Td (by the Safety Officer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 497.4 Td (The investigation process involves:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 482.9 Td (-   Reviewing all collected evidence and witness statements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 468.4 Td (-   Analyzing operational procedures and maintenance records.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 453.9 Td (-   Identifying gaps in training, equipment, or communication.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 439.4 Td (-   Developing corrective actions with assigned responsibilities and deadlines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 410.4 Td (Findings must be documented in the incident report file. Corrective actions are tracked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 395.9 Td (until closure to ensure effectiveness.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 353.9 Td (Lessons Learned) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 339.4 Td (The value of reporting lies in the dissemination of knowledge. Each vessel must submit at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 324.9 Td (least 2 near-miss reports per month to maintain a proactive safety culture. These reports,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 310.4 Td (along with serious incident findings, are reviewed by the company's Safety Department. Key) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 295.9 Td (lessons learned are distributed to all vessels via Safety Bulletins and integrated into) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 281.4 Td (training programs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 252.4 Td (Crew members are encouraged to participate in safety meetings where recent incidents are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 237.9 Td (discussed anonymously if necessary. This fosters an open environment where concerns can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 223.4 Td (raised without fear of reprisal. Regular audits will verify compliance with reporting quotas) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 208.9 Td (and the quality of submitted reports. Continuous feedback loops ensure that lessons learned) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 194.4 Td (translate into tangible improvements in shipboard operations and risk management.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (SMS-15 Incident and Near-Miss Reporting \(fictional\) - page 2 of 2) Tj ET
